<div class="jn-stack">
  <p class="jn-lead">Routine coding is increasingly automated. Build the depth to design, optimize, and verify the whole system.</p>

  <p class="jn-colhead"><b>AI pressure</b> &nbsp;Five layers to understand</p>
  <div class="jn-layers">
    <div class="jn-pressure" aria-hidden="true"><span>From software to silicon</span></div>
    <div class="jn-layer-list">
      <div class="jn-layer" style="--c: var(--l1)">
        <div class="jn-ico"><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i><small>01</small></div>
        <div class="jn-top">
          <p class="jn-name">Software &amp; applications</p>
          <span class="jn-tag">Task automation</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jn-items">Apps &middot; services &middot; scripts &middot; tests</p>
        <p class="jn-desc">Routine coding faces automation; entry-level roles face pressure.<sup>[1]</sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="jn-layer" style="--c: var(--l2)">
        <div class="jn-ico"><i class="fa-solid fa-sitemap"></i><small>02</small></div>
        <div class="jn-top">
          <p class="jn-name">Compilers</p>
          <span class="jn-tag">Optimization by AI</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jn-items">Code generation &middot; optimization passes &middot; auto-tuning</p>
        <p class="jn-desc">AI learns compiler optimizations and tunes generated code.<sup>[2]</sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="jn-layer" style="--c: var(--l3)">
        <div class="jn-ico"><i class="fa-solid fa-table-cells-large"></i><small>03</small></div>
        <div class="jn-top">
          <p class="jn-name">Kernels &amp; runtime</p>
          <span class="jn-tag">Performance pressure</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jn-items">CUDA / Triton &middot; parallelism &middot; memory systems</p>
        <p class="jn-desc">AI generates GPU kernels; correctness and speed need testing.<sup>[3]</sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="jn-frontier"><span>AI frontier today &mdash; still moving down &darr;</span></div>
      <div class="jn-layer" style="--c: var(--l4)">
        <div class="jn-ico"><i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project"></i><small>04</small></div>
        <div class="jn-top">
          <p class="jn-name">Computer architecture</p>
          <span class="jn-tag">System trade-offs</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jn-items">Accelerators &middot; dataflows &middot; interconnects &middot; memory hierarchies</p>
        <p class="jn-desc">AI explores architectures; goals and trade-offs guide the search.<sup>[4]</sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="jn-layer" style="--c: var(--l5)">
        <div class="jn-ico"><i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i><small>05</small></div>
        <div class="jn-top">
          <p class="jn-name">Digital IC design</p>
          <span class="jn-tag">Physical constraints</span>
        </div>
        <p class="jn-items">RTL &middot; verification &middot; synthesis &middot; physical design</p>
        <p class="jn-desc">AI assists RTL and chip layout; verification remains essential.<sup>[5]</sup></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="jn-colhead">Why deeper expertise matters</p>
  <div class="jn-why">
    <div>
      <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-database"></i>Less accessible training data</h4>
      <p>Hardware data is less abundant; much design knowledge is proprietary.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i>Physical constraints</h4>
      <p>Timing, power, and area must meet real implementation limits.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>Costly hardware mistakes</h4>
      <p>Silicon errors can require expensive, time-consuming redesigns.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-nodes"></i>Cross-layer judgment</h4>
      <p>Connect workloads, algorithms, and hardware to choose the right trade-offs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="jn-banner">
    <strong>Go deeper. Connect the layers. Engineer with AI.</strong>
    <span>Software &rarr; Compilers &rarr; Kernels &rarr; Architecture &rarr; Digital IC design</span>
  </div>
  <div class="jn-foot">
    <em>A learning strategy, not a job-loss forecast. AI is advancing at every layer.</em>
    <span><b>Sources</b> [1] Stanford 2025 &nbsp;[2] Meta 2024 &nbsp;[3] KernelBench 2025 &nbsp;[4] ArchGym 2023 &nbsp;[5] DeepMind 2021</span>
  </div>
</div>
